      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing today, with 14 cm of fresh snow overnight and excellent mountain coverage. The snow is expected to remain cold and dry up high, becoming more spring-like lower down. The mountain is currently -6°C, with 13 km/h winds and 23 km/h gusts; the day is expected to remain mainly fine as cloud clears. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow’s Quad are open, while Wells Pipe Platter is closed. Main Basin and Captains are open, with 10/10 terrain areas open; Olympic Pipe is closed, and the Big Bucks jump line has Jump 0 only. Issued: 10:35 am, 17 Sep. The access road is chain-free, although chains must always be carried, and an active road-hazard advisory remains in effect. Car Park A is full, while Car Parks B, C, The Yard, Valley View and The Pines have availability. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
