      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with 17 cm of fresh snow overnight, including 17 cm at the top of Home Basin, 25 cm at the top of Saddle and 7 cm at the base. The new snow is light and dry higher up but sits on a wet snowpack on the lower mountain after yesterday's rain, producing excellent skiing in places but more variable spring conditions lower down. It is currently -4°C, with 11 km/h winds and 18 km/h gusts, and fine weather is forecast. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Home Basin, Lower Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are open. Saddle Track is closed from 11am, Motatapu Chutes remain closed, and the Terrain Park is delayed. Issued: 11:09 am, 17 Sep. The access road is chain-free, but all vehicles must carry chains, with a current road-hazard advisory. The Saddle Track closure is due to glide-slab concerns above the Saddle access; the Saddle Quad continues running. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
